\pard\plain \sl288\slmult1\ltrch\loch {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 I know you don\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8217\'92t want to debase yourself by doing what it takes to succeed, but the money is easy. It is }{\f2\fs24\b0\i1 sitting}{\f1\fs24\b0\i0  there for the taking. People }{\f2\fs24\b0\i1 want}{\f1\fs24\b0\i0  to give it to you. A young man such as you, I cannot understand why you won\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8217\'92t even try. Do you not want a woman on your arm? A house? Respect?\u8221\'94 }
\par\plain \f1\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 A show of hard thinking}
\par\plain \f1\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain \f1\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 He picked up a spoon and stirred his leechy porridge. He took one bite of it, then immediately clutched his jaw and winced. \loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92ve a troublesome tooth,\u8221\'94 he said before spitting the glob of unswallowed mush back into its bowl. Then he sighed, because nothing on the table could accommodate toothache. On Vigram\u8217\'92s second bite, his tongue slipped, and the pain had him talking out the side of his cheek in an odd drawl. And now it hurt to hear the man speak, in more ways than one.}
\par\plain \f1\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 He pounded his table with his fat hand, and one of his slaves popped out of the kitchen. The slave carried two steaming plates of Meskalimi leech, and then another came, ferrying more incomprehensible plates and bowls of leech.}
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 \line }
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 The fat swerve of his bottom lip was a baited hook. }
\par\pard\plain \ltrch\loch \f1\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain \f1\fs24\b0\i0
\par\pard\plain \sl288\slmult1\ltrch\loch {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 At least ten other artists had tried to teach Vigram how to paint, and they\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8217\'92d all been fired. It was Mandri\u8217\'92s turn today. He\u8217\'92d come because he needed the money, but there was also a little motivating curiosity, because why had all the others failed, or given up, when the money was so good? A few, it was rumored, were so discouraged by the time of their final lesson, that they packed their bags and took off for the other side of the world, never to be seen again. }
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 As it turns out, there was no great mystery: no one wanted to teach }
\par\plain \f1\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain \f1\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain \f1\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0\i0  The man claimed that he didn\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8217\'92t normally go into the temple, because that meant he\u8217\'92d have to listen to a dullard speak, but he\u8217\'92d gone, and now his elbows were on the table so that his hands could help communicate his big ideas. These were delicate gestures, as if he were subjecting Mandri to a kind of surgery where the degeneracy of this fallen world was being extracted from his mind by means of interrogation.}}